<article class="env-lemma" id="0H1Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H1Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0H1Q">68.7.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $U \to X$ be an étale morphism from a scheme to $X$. Assume $u, u' \in |U|$ map to the same point $x$ of $|X|$, and $u' \leadsto u$. If $X$ is locally Noetherian, then $u = u'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The discussion in Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/01J5" data-tag="01J5">26.13</a> shows that $\mathcal{O}_{U, u'}$ is a localization of the Noetherian local ring $\mathcal{O}_{U, u}$. By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BAM" data-tag="0BAM">66.10.1</a> we have $\dim (\mathcal{O}_{U, u}) = \dim (\mathcal{O}_{U, u'})$. By dimension theory for Noetherian local rings we conclude $u = u'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>